  "note": "`display: grid-lanes`, `inline-grid-lanes` and the older `grid-template-rows: masonry` (or `grid-template-columns: masonry`) work: lanes are columns or rows, items go to the shortest lane in order, spans, explicit lanes and intrinsic lane sizes work, checked against Chromium. Missing: the `flow-tolerance` property (ties are always within 1em), `dense` back-filling, subgrids inside lanes, and lanes split across pages or columns.",
